---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/siteConfig';
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`Terms of Service | ${siteConfig.metadata.siteName}`}
  description="The terms that cover commissioning custom music from Seram Sound — scope, payment, revisions, usage rights, and confidentiality."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  lastUpdated="June 12, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover what you can expect when you commission custom music from
    {siteConfig.name}, and what I ask of you in return. They're meant to be clear and fair —
    not full of fine print. Every project also comes with its own written agreement, and where
    that agreement differs from these terms, the agreement wins.
  </p>

  <h2>Services</h2>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.name} provides original, custom music composition and production for film,
    documentary, branded content, and other short-form work. The exact deliverables, format,
    and timeline for your project are defined in your project quote and agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Quotes &amp; project scope</h2>
  <p>
    Each project is quoted individually based on its length, complexity, timeline, and licensing
    needs. The quote you approve defines the agreed scope. Work that falls outside that scope —
    additional cues, added length, or expanded usage rights — may be quoted separately before it
    proceeds.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>50% deposit</strong> is required before composition begins, with the remaining balance
    due upon final delivery. Final files are released once payment is complete. Deposits cover work
    already underway and are non-refundable once composition has started.
  </p>

  <h2>Revisions</h2>
  <p>
    Up to <strong>two rounds of revisions</strong> are included in every quote so we can refine the
    score until it serves your edit. Further revisions, or changes that go beyond the original creative
    direction, can be added at an agreed rate.
  </p>

  <h2>Timelines</h2>
  <p>
    Delivery timelines are set per project and built around your deadline — a short spot moves quickly,
    while a longer-form score needs more time. Timelines assume timely feedback and materials from you;
    delays on either side may shift the delivery date. I'll always communicate clearly if a schedule needs
    to change.
  </p>

  <h2>Usage rights &amp; ownership</h2>
  <p>
    On final payment, you receive a license to use the delivered music for the project and usage scope
    described in your agreement. Unless your agreement states otherwise, I retain authorship and ownership
    of the underlying composition and master recordings. If you need broader or exclusive rights, we'll
    define and price that up front.
  </p>

  <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    I treat unreleased projects as confidential and won't share work-in-progress publicly before your
    release. If your project requires a non-disclosure agreement, I'm happy to sign one. I'd love to feature
    completed work in my portfolio once it's public — but only with your okay.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    I take pride in delivering work that fits your project, but I can't guarantee specific commercial
    outcomes. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.name}'s liability for any claim related
    to a project is limited to the amount you paid for that project.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated occasionally; the "last updated" date above reflects the current version.
    The terms in effect when you commission a project are the ones that apply to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
